# Four bots in deathmatch on LibreQuake's start map (L-87, BOT-9.2): the server has five slots,
# the player's and the bots', and deathmatch 1, as `-listen 5` gives one. In CI (`cargo xtask
# scenario xtask/fixtures/scenarios/bots-deathmatch.scenario --repeat 2 -- -basedir
# "$QS_TEST_ASSETS/librequake-lite"`) it plays twice and must give the same result each time
# (SCN-2.5): the same frags for each bot, which a change to the bots' minds may change and
# this file then records again. The player stands where it spawned.
map start
seed 1996
engine -listen
engine 5
frames 4
console addbot 1
console addbot 1
console addbot 1
console addbot 1
frames 2880
expect field 2 netname == "Ash"
expect field 5 netname == "Dune"
expect field 2 frags == 1
expect field 3 frags == 1
expect field 4 frags == 0
expect field 5 frags == -1
